<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 Unit 4 Lesson 17 Four Operations"><h2>Original 2021 warm-up: multiply by10</h2><p>2×40=2×4×10 true;2×40=8×10 true;3×50=15×10 true;3×40=7×10 false (120 ≠ 70).</p><h2>Source party context: generate your own questions</h2><p>There are142 guests,94 in roomA,6 equal tables in roomB, and4 silverware pieces plus1 plate per guest. Write questions. Original teacher focus: <strong>(142−94)÷6=g=8 guests/table</strong>; equivalent (g×6)+94=142.</p><h2>Original three Party Problems</h2><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Equation with unknown</th><th>Answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Kiran156 rings + Friday Kiran and2 friends each9</td><td>r=156+(3×9)</td><td>183 rings</td></tr><tr><td>Mai168 muffins,104 basket,8 boxes</td><td>m=(168−104)÷8</td><td>8 per box</td></tr><tr><td>184 cups,3 tables×8 people take one cup</td><td>c=184−(3×8)</td><td>160 remain</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Original student summary4×30=120,7×13=91,3×28=84. Independent equations, teacher reviews letter unknown and parenthesis sequencing. Source five images inspected; no publisher original assets embedded. <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-4/lesson-17/lesson.html">2021 teacher lesson</a></p></section>
